# Lab Setup

## Host

- Ubuntu server on an MSI Cyborg 15 laptop
- Virtualization: VirtualBox
- Network: isolated host-only network, so targets are separated from the rest of my network and not exposed to the internet

## Attacker Machine

### Kali Linux
- Attack box, running in VirtualBox on the same host-only network as the targets
- Used for: Nmap, Burp Suite, Metasploit, and other testing tools against the targets below

## Targets

### OWASP Juice Shop
- Intentionally insecure web application
- Used for: XSS, SQL injection, broken access control, authentication flaws

### crAPI (Completely Ridiculous API)
- Intentionally vulnerable API
- Used for: BOLA/IDOR, broken authentication, mass assignment, excessive data exposure

### Metasploitable 2
- Intentionally vulnerable Linux VM
- Used for: Nmap scanning, service enumeration, Metasploit practice
